    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d369">

                <pb facs="0508" n="500" xml:id="pg500"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2373: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Military Attaché in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Shipp</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the War Department
                    </hi><anchor n="94" xml:id="d369-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-10-06">October 6,
                        1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Within 6 months according to Japanese Military Attaché in Madrid the United
                    States and Japan would be at war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shipp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d369-f1" n="94" type="source" xml:id="d369-f1-content">
                <p>Received at the War Department October 6, 1941, 6:48 p.m.; paraphrase received in
                    Department of State on October 8. Noted by the Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
